From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 31] ggml-sycl: Q8_0_SOA, a q8_0 expert layout and its one-token MoE matvec

The SOA layout of patches 09 / 17 ([codes][scales] per 2-D slice, codes 16-byte aligned) for q8_0: 32 code bytes and
a 2-byte scale per block. The one-token MoE matvec takes 16-byte half blocks, LPR lanes per row (8 for rows of 20
blocks: no idle lane), four sub-groups per work-group; the stock kernel runs one 16-lane work-group per row and reads
a q8_0 expert-down at ~85 GB/s. GGML_SYCL_Q8_SOA_LPR=16|8|4 forces the lanes per row. Also: the upload / read-back
conversions take the block size (18 or 34 bytes), a dequantize for the multi-token path, and patch 30's CPY back to
the file's blocks for Q8_0_SOA.

